  wax-mb is a port of the Wax compiler from OCaml to MoonBit. It is written
  against the reference implementation as its specification, and its test
  corpus (test/corpus/) and expected outputs (test/golden/) are derived from
  that project's sources and produced by its binary. The pinned upstream
  commit is recorded in tools/reference.json.

  This repository also REDISTRIBUTES an unmodified upstream build of that
  compiler, as the release named by `mirror_release` in tools/reference.json.
  Upstream publishes only a floating 'edge' asset, rebuilt on every push, so
  the exact build these goldens were produced by is otherwise unobtainable
  once it moves. The copy is byte-for-byte the artifact ocsigen/wax released
  for the pinned commit -- tools/fetch-reference.sh verifies its sha256
  against the pin before installing it, from either source -- and it is
  redistributed under the same Apache License, Version 2.0.

